## 4. PATIENT MOBILE APP (§4)

For every module below implement: the inputs/validations, the numbered flow, the outputs, the business rules, and make each acceptance criterion an automated test.

### 4.1 Home dashboard
- **Inputs:** Patient/account ID (authenticated session; show only own data); Next appointment (doctor, time, status; hide if none); Pending bill / report alert (amount/due date or report-ready; deep-link to detail); Quick actions (Book appointment, lab test, medicines, pay bill, reports, emergency SOS).
- **Flow:** authenticate & load profile/permissions → fetch upcoming appointment, outstanding balance, report notifications → render actionable cards + bottom navigation (**Home, Visits, Records, Payments**) → on selection open workflow **preserving context**.
- **Outputs:** dashboard cards (appointment, bill, report status); navigation; in-app alerts (sample values clearly marked illustrative).
- **Rules:** Emergency action always prominent, never obstructed by promotions; clear empty state when no appointment/bill/new report.
- **Acceptance:** Patient sees only own information unless an authorized **dependent-profile** feature is enabled.

### 4.2 Sign-in, registration, account recovery
- **Inputs:** User ID/mobile (required, normalize + validate format); Password + confirm (required at registration, must match); Email (validate; used for updates/receipts as configured); OTP/verification code via SMS/email provider (**expiry, attempt limits, resend cooldown**); Consent (store consent **text, version, timestamp**).
- **Flow:** choose Sign in / Create account / Forgot password → registration: user ID, mobile, email, password, review privacy notice/consent → verify mobile by OTP if enabled; validate uniqueness + password policy → create account, show confirmation, route to sign-in or home → recovery: verify identity via configured channel, set new password, **invalidate appropriate sessions**.
- **Outputs:** account/authenticated session; success/failure message with retry path; password-reset confirmation with **no disclosure of whether an account exists**.
- **Rules:** Recommended: OTP for registration/reset, staff MFA, biometric sign-in, session timeout, device management. Error messages must not expose sensitive account details.
- **Acceptance:** Duplicate user IDs/mobiles handled without duplicate accounts; invalid, expired or reused OTPs rejected **and logged**.

### 4.3 Find a doctor
- **Inputs:** Hospital/branch (required where multiple); Specialty (filter against configured specialties); Doctor name (partial match); Filters (fee, day, home visit — only show supported filters/data); Doctor profile (photo, degrees/training, expertise, experience, working days, fee, rating where available).
- **Flow:** open Find a doctor → select branch + specialty or enter name; optional filters → directory search with **pagination** → open profile, review, choose appointment action.
- **Outputs:** doctor cards + pagination; profile with booking action; empty state with no-match message and option to change filters.
- **Rules:** Never display unavailable/unverified profile attributes as confirmed.
- **Acceptance:** Filters combine consistently; pagination never repeats or omits results.

### 4.4 Appointment scheduling & confirmation
- **Inputs:** Doctor/specialty (active & bookable); Date + time slot (available, within booking rules); Visit type (in-person/video only where enabled); Fee & policy (displayed before confirmation); Payment method (supported only; **never store raw card data**).
- **Flow:** select doctor, view dates/slots → choose slot; system **rechecks availability and temporarily holds it during payment** → review doctor, branch, date/time, visit type, fee, cancellation/reschedule policy → confirm and initiate payment when required → process payment callback/result; **prevent duplicate booking; reconcile pending outcomes** → show appointment reference, receipt/status, add-to-calendar action; enable view/reschedule/cancel per policy.
- **Outputs:** appointment status (**Confirmed / Pending payment / Failed-Cancelled**); unique booking ID; payment receipt when applicable; confirmation/reminder notifications to patient **and relevant staff**.
- **Rules:** handle unavailable slots, payment failure/cancellation, duplicate submissions, **late callbacks**. Reschedule/cancellation windows and no-show rules are **admin-configurable** (need business confirmation).
- **Acceptance:** A slot can never be double-booked (DB-level uniqueness/locking); patient always gets a clear final status and reference even if payment is pending.

### 4.5 Medical records & health wallet
- **Inputs:** Patient identity (secure match); Record category (All, prescriptions, lab, imaging, summaries); Record metadata (date, source, status, units); Download request (authorized PDF / secure download).
- **Flow:** open Records, choose category/record → retrieve only authorized records for current access context → display source, date, status, units → secure PDF download where supported; **log access/download**.
- **Outputs:** record list (prescriptions, lab reports, radiology, discharge summaries, vitals/allergies, encounter summaries); view/download document; report-ready notification where configured.
- **Rules:** Recommended additions: allergy/chronic-condition history, family history, secure document upload. **Unreviewed results must never be presented as a diagnosis.**
- **Acceptance:** Access is patient-scoped and audited; unavailable records show a clear status.

### 4.6 Billing & payments
- **Inputs:** Invoice/account (invoice ID, line items, due date, taxes/charges, balance); Payment method (UPI/card/net banking/wallet only if configured); Promo code (validate eligibility + expiry); Transaction response from gateway (success/pending/failure/cancellation).
- **Flow:** open Payments, select invoice or account statement → review amount, due date, details, options → apply eligible promo, recalculate total → redirect/tokenize via approved provider, receive result → update payment ledger **idempotently**; reconcile gateway callback; generate receipt → PDF receipt and refund status where applicable.
- **Outputs:** invoice view/statement; status (Paid/Pending/Failed/Cancelled); receipt with transaction reference + downloadable PDF; updated ledger + reconciliation record.
- **Rules:** duplicate callbacks and retries handled idempotently; payment credentials stay with provider, **never store raw card data**; refund and reconciliation ownership are configurable (need confirmation).
- **Acceptance:** Amount paid cannot exceed outstanding unless **advance payment** is explicitly enabled; every transaction has a unique reference and audit trail.

### 4.7 Laboratory test booking
- **Inputs:** Test/package (active, priced); Collection mode (at hospital or home if available); Date/slot (available for mode/branch); Patient/order details (required clinical/order details per test).
- **Flow:** search/select test or package → choose collection mode, branch/address, slot → review instructions, price, details; pay if required → create lab order and notify lab/collection team → show order + report status; notify when report ready.
- **Outputs:** lab order (reference, slot, status); operations queue entry for lab/collection team; report appears in Records when released.
- **Rules:** home collection depends on serviceability + operational confirmation; report release/review workflow configurable (validate with lab stakeholders).
- **Acceptance:** Unavailable slots cannot be booked and patient can pick another; status mirrors source system and **never implies clinical interpretation**.

### 4.8 Pharmacy, prescriptions & refills
- **Inputs:** Prescription (medicine, dosage, frequency, duration, prescriber); Refill request (subject to prescription validity + approval); Allergy information (display known allergies); Order/delivery details (only if pharmacy fulfilment enabled).
- **Flow:** open Medicines, view prescriptions + dosage → review reminders if configured → request refill/order where enabled → pharmacy validates prescription, stock, eligibility → update request/order status, notify patient.
- **Outputs:** prescription view; refill status (**Submitted / Pending / Approved / Rejected**); pharmacy review queue; allergy alert.
- **Rules:** refills subject to pharmacist approval + policy; inventory/fulfilment features behind feature flags.
- **Acceptance:** Patient **cannot alter prescribed dosage**; refill requests are traceable and reviewed.

### 4.9 Emergency help & ambulance request
- **Inputs:** Emergency type/callback (confirm callback number); Location (device or manual entry, permission-based); Patient context (minimum necessary data); Dispatch response (only statuses supplied by dispatch).
- **Flow:** select Emergency SOS or Request ambulance → show **emergency call fallback** and clarify it's not a routine appointment → request location permission or accept manual location; confirm callback number → submit to configured dispatch workflow → show request reference and received/assigned status when available → notify patient and authorized case-management/dispatch users.
- **Outputs:** emergency request (reference + details); dispatch queue entry; status (received/assigned/updated **only when confirmed by dispatch**).
- **Rules:** clear emergency-call fallback; location sharing requires permission; **never claim dispatch/ETA without integration confirmation**.
- **Acceptance:** Emergency request is visually distinct and accessible; if connection fails, immediate fallback instructions appear.

