## 5. HOSPITAL STAFF PORTAL & CORE OPERATIONS (§5)

### 5.1 Staff dashboard
- **Inputs:** user role/branch (controls widgets + data scope); date/department filters (validate allowed range/scope); operational data from patient, appointment, bed, pharmacy, lab, billing, claims (show **source and refresh time**).
- **Flow:** authenticate, resolve role/branch → load permitted KPIs + queues → apply filters, refresh → navigate to detail screens and authorized export.
- **Outputs:** dashboard (patients, appointments, beds available, revenue, operational queues); alerts (bed occupancy, lab turnaround, pharmacy expiry, claims, exceptions); authorized report export.
- **Rules:** sample values illustrative; clearly distinguish live / delayed / mock data.
- **Acceptance:** users cannot view metrics outside assigned branch/role scope.

### 5.2 Patient registration & front office
- **Inputs:** demographics (required identity/contact fields; **duplicate matching**); visit details (department, doctor, visit type, reason as configured); contact/communication (consent, preferred channel).
- **Flow:** search existing patient by approved identifiers → if none, capture demographics, create record → register visit, schedule or check in → route request to department, update status.
- **Outputs:** unique Patient ID; appointment/check-in record; front-office queue with assigned request + status.
- **Rules:** avoid duplicate records, provide **escalation path for uncertain matches**; restrict patient data by role.
- **Acceptance:** required fields validated; every registration/change audited.

### 5.3 Admissions, beds & discharge
- **Inputs:** patient/admission (patient ID, reason, case); assessment (service/ward, care needs); bed request (VIP, AC, Non-AC or configured type); charges/advance; discharge data (summary, sign-offs, outstanding balance).
- **Flow:** register admission, assess service/ward → check bed availability, allocate → record case manager + admission details, update occupancy → during stay record care and charges → complete clinical discharge summary and billing clearance/sign-off → release bed, **trigger cleaning task, update availability after readiness workflow**.
- **Outputs:** admission record (Admission ID, ward/bed); bed board (occupied/available); discharge summary, bill, status; housekeeping cleaning task.
- **Rules:** OT, ICU, emergency triage, nursing notes, shift handover = recommended extensions (build as optional modules/flags); bed readiness may depend on housekeeping inspection.
- **Acceptance:** a bed cannot be assigned to overlapping active admissions; discharge/release auditable and availability updated consistently.

### 5.4 Pharmacy inventory & billing
- **Inputs:** medicine catalogue (category, brand, item, unit, price); inventory (quantity, batch, expiry); prescription (patient, medicine, dosage); dispensing/billing (quantity, charges).
- **Flow:** maintain categories/brands/inventory → receive prescription or authorized sale → check stock + safety alerts → dispense, record quantity/batch, generate bill → update inventory + financial ledger; alert on low stock/expiry.
- **Outputs:** inventory with movement history; patient-linked dispensing record; medicine invoice; low-stock/expiry alert queue.
- **Rules:** expiry alerts and refill workflow recommended; inventory changes preserve traceability.
- **Acceptance:** dispensing cannot exceed available stock without an **authorized exception**.

### 5.5 Laboratory, radiology & diagnostics
- **Inputs:** test order (patient, test, priority, clinical context); specimen/appointment (collection details, status); result (values, units, reference ranges, review status); imaging (images + report where PACS integrated).
- **Flow:** receive + prioritize order → schedule/collect specimen or perform imaging → record result, validate/review per lab workflow → release to authorized patient/staff views → update turnaround metrics, notify patient.
- **Outputs:** work queue (pending tests, collection tasks); reviewed/released report; patient record link (report + image); analytics (test status, turnaround).
- **Rules:** analyzer/PACS integration recommended (needs technical discovery); clinical review + result-release rules configurable.
- **Acceptance:** released reports show status, date, source, units where relevant.

### 5.6 Blood bank
- **Inputs:** stock item (group, component, unit, collection/expiry date, storage status); donor record (details, screening status); reservation/issue (patient/case, compatibility, authorized release); external availability (source, quantity, timestamp, confirmation, ETA).
- **Flow:** maintain stock + donors; **flag outdated/unused stock** → receive request, check internal compatible inventory → if insufficient, search connected blood banks/hospitals, compare **confirmed** availability → obtain required approval; submit transfer/collection request → record provider confirmation, receipt, screening/compatibility checks, authorized issue → update stock/reservation/transfer records + audit.
- **Outputs:** inventory by group/component/expiry; external request (provider reference, status, ETA); traceable issue/transfer with recipient/case; alerts (low stock, near-expiry, stockout).
- **Rules:** compatibility, screening, authorized release follow approved hospital workflow; availability always shows **source + last-updated time**.
- **Acceptance:** **no blood unit issued without required authorization and traceability.**

### 5.7 Billing, finance, insurance & payroll
- **Inputs:** charge/transaction (service, amount, patient/account, reference); payment/advance (method, amount, transaction ID, status); insurance case (policy, eligibility, pre-auth, documents, claim status); payroll inputs (staff, salary components, attendance, adjustments).
- **Flow:** generate invoice from approved services/charges → record advance/payment, reconcile gateway or cashier transaction → maintain statements, income/expenses, authorized adjustments → insurance: verify policy, submit pre-auth/claim, track queries, approval, rejection, settlement → process payroll with authorized inputs; generate controlled reports.
- **Outputs:** invoice/statement/due-received balances; payment ledger with references + reconciliation status; insurance claim timeline, outstanding amount, settlement; payslips/reports for authorized users.
- **Rules:** separate clinical and financial permissions; audit history for all financial adjustments; insurer/TPA and payroll integrations validated separately.
- **Acceptance:** all financial changes attributed and auditable; restricted data role-limited.

