## 6. ENGAGEMENT & COMMUNICATION MODULES (§6)

### 6.1 Careers & job portal
- **Inputs:** vacancy (role, department, location, employment type, experience, opening/closing dates); candidate profile (contact, CV, certificates, professional registration if applicable); interview (schedule, interviewers, feedback); application status: **Submitted → Under Review → Shortlisted → Interview Scheduled → Selected / Not Selected**.
- **Flow:** HR creates/edits vacancy → submits for approval/publication → candidate searches/filters, opens details → submits application + attachments, system generates reference → HR reviews, shortlists, schedules interview; interviewers record feedback → HR updates status, tracks offer/appointment letter → notify candidate via consented, configured channels; retain records per policy.
- **Outputs:** published listing + closing status; application reference + status; recruitment pipeline + interview calendar; notifications.
- **Rules:** optional employee referral, internships, training, fellowships; candidate data retention + hiring approvals configurable.
- **Acceptance:** closed/expired vacancies cannot accept applications; status history retained.

### 6.2 Announcements & notices
- **Inputs:** content (title, body, category, attachments, priority); audience (all staff, role, department, branch, or patients); schedule (publish + expiry); approval (required for critical/emergency).
- **Flow:** publisher drafts, selects audience/category/priority → submit for approval where required → approver approves / rejects / requests changes → publish to portal/app/notice board + send configured notifications → track delivery, views, acknowledgement; export report.
- **Outputs:** published notice with expiry; push/email/SMS as configured; acknowledgement report (audience, delivery/view/ack status).
- **Rules:** emergency broadcast restricted to authorized users. Categories: **General, Urgent, Clinical/Safety, HR, Training, Maintenance, Events, Patient Information**.
- **Acceptance:** expired notices never shown as current; critical acknowledgements reportable.

### 6.3 Advertisements & promotions
- **Inputs:** campaign (title, description, banner, destination, audience, dates); offer terms (promo code, eligibility, validity, terms); approval (content + clinical claims review); analytics (impressions, clicks, enquiries, bookings).
- **Flow:** create campaign with approved content/offer terms → select branch, audience, schedule; submit for approval → approver reviews; approved campaign published + scheduled → auto-stop at expiry or pause/cancel by authorized user → track privacy-conscious engagement metrics.
- **Outputs:** approved published promotion; patient-app display **clearly labelled "Advertisement / Sponsored"**; performance report.
- **Rules:** no misleading medical claims; never interfere with emergency/care workflows; avoid identifiable health data for ad targeting; apply consent/privacy rules.
- **Acceptance:** only approved campaigns publish; expired campaigns stop automatically.

