## 7. EXTERNAL COORDINATION MODULES (§7)

**Shared request lifecycle (build as one reusable state machine):**
`Draft → Submitted → Approval pending → Provider processing → Confirmed → Fulfilled → Closed`
Exception states: `Rejected, Unavailable, Delayed, Cancelled, Escalated`.

### 7.1 Dashboard & request management
- **Inputs:** category (Blood, supplier, housekeeping, insurance, manpower); details (need, quantity/capacity, location, urgency, deadline, attachments); provider availability (API/portal/email/manual; source, last updated, quantity, ETA, confirmation); approval (role/value/urgency threshold).
- **Flow:** authorized user creates request → unique request ID → system checks internal stock/roster + configured external sources → show options with source, freshness, location, quantity/capacity, confirmation → compare, obtain approvals → submit request/order/claim/task to provider, record provider reference → track response, ETA, exceptions, communication → record receipt/deployment/completion/outcome, update related module, close with audit.
- **Outputs:** dashboard (open, awaiting approval, confirmed, exception counts); request record (timeline, attachments, approvals, communications); fulfilment outcome + updated inventory/roster/status.
- **Rules:** label stale/unconfirmed availability; failed integrations create **visible exception + manual follow-up path**; prevent or flag duplicate submissions.
- **Acceptance:** every request has unique ID, requester, category, priority, timestamps, status; search/filter by **branch, category, provider, owner, priority, status**.

### 7.2 Supplier catalogue & purchase request
- **Inputs:** item (category, specification, unit, quantity); delivery (branch/store, requested date); supplier (approval status, price list, availability, lead time, freshness); purchase request (budget/department, attachments); receipt (quantity, batch/serial, quality check, discrepancy).
- **Flow:** search item/category + delivery location → compare approved suppliers (price, stock, lead time, verification) → add item/quantity, submit purchase request → budget/department approval, create PO → track dispatch/delivery; receive goods + quality check → record returns/warranty/service requests; **match invoice and payment (3-way match)**.
- **Outputs:** PR/PO IDs, supplier, approved amount; dispatch/ETA + goods receipt; stock updated after accepted receipt; matched invoice/payment status.
- **Rules:** if real-time vendor integration unavailable, support portal/email/manual confirmation; keep supplier performance + issue history.
- **Acceptance:** PO cannot be submitted without required approval; receipt discrepancies recorded.

### 7.3 Cleaning & housekeeping
- **Inputs:** task (location, type, priority, checklist); assignment (staff/agency, shift, roster); execution (start/end, checklist, notes); inspection (pass/fail, sign-off or reopen reason).
- **Flow:** create task by ward/room/theatre/department + priority → assign staff/agency + shift, notify → staff marks In Progress, records checklist/timestamps → mark Completed, submit for inspection → supervisor inspects; **pass → room/bed Ready; fail → reopen/escalate** → notify front office/nursing; retain audit.
- **Outputs:** task board (**Assigned, In Progress, Awaiting Inspection, Completed, Reopened**); room readiness; audit (checklist, timestamps, assignee, supervisor sign-off).
- **Rules:** missed tasks escalate per priority/SLA; shift handover and maintenance requests where configured.
- **Acceptance:** room cannot be marked Ready before required inspection passes.

### 7.4 Insurance / TPA pre-authorisation & claims
- **Inputs:** patient/admission ID; insurer/TPA + policy (member ID, coverage, eligibility); estimate + documents (clinical notes, reports); claim timeline (reference, query, approval/rejection, settlement).
- **Flow:** select patient/admission + insurer/TPA → verify policy/eligibility, record result/reference → prepare pre-auth with estimate + documents → submit via API/portal or controlled manual process → track query, assign owner, upload response, resubmit → submit final claim; track approval/rejection/settlement; notify billing + case manager.
- **Outputs:** insurance case (verified policy, auth status); claim timeline (submission, query, response, settlement); billing updates (approved coverage, patient responsibility, outstanding).
- **Rules:** sensitive clinical/insurance data to authorized roles only; keep insurer reference, documents, response dates, query owner, audit history.
- **Acceptance:** every claim event timestamped and attributable; query ownership visible.

### 7.5 Manpower & staffing agency
- **Inputs:** staffing need (role, headcount, location, shift, duration, urgency, qualifications); agency (availability, quote, service area); credential checks (licences, qualifications, verification status); deployment (roster, attendance, replacement, timesheet, invoice).
- **Flow:** create request, check approved agency availability → compare candidate/agency response + quote → approval; verify credentials/onboarding → confirm deployment, create roster → track attendance, shift handover, replacements → approve timesheet, reconcile agency invoice.
- **Outputs:** request ID/status; verified personnel, roster, attendance; timesheet/invoice review record.
- **Rules:** clinical duties only for qualified, credential-verified personnel; retain approvals + deployment history.
- **Acceptance:** no clinical deployment before required credential checks and approvals.

### 7.6 Centralized availability & coordination
- **Inputs:** resource (stock, service, staff, capacity); provider metadata (source, location, last-updated, response/lead time); request (need, quantity, priority, destination); confirmation (Confirmed / Partial / Unavailable + ETA).
- **Flow:** check internal inventory/roster **first** → query providers via API/webhook or fallback portal/email/phone → normalize + display options with source, timestamp, capacity, location, confirmation → compare, approvals → submit, track confirmation/fulfilment → update stock, room readiness, claim or roster records + audit.
- **Outputs:** cross-provider availability view with freshness + confirmation labels; request tracking (status, provider ref, ETA, exceptions); operational updates.
- **Rules:** **never present stale or unconfirmed data as live**; availability depends on provider agreements/technical capability.
- **Acceptance:** each result identifies source and last update; stale data visibly flagged.

