## 8. ADMIN, REPORTING, SECURITY, INTEGRATIONS (§8)

### 8.1 Administration & RBAC
- **Inputs:** user/staff profile (identity, department, branch, status); role/permission (module/action/data scope); configuration (departments, service catalogue, fees, settings, workflow thresholds); approval policy (approver, threshold, escalation).
- **Flow:** create/update user, assign branch/department → assign role + least-privilege permissions → configure module settings + approval rules → periodic access review; deactivate when no longer required.
- **Outputs:** effective access profile; updated reference data/workflow rules; audit (user, action, timestamp, change details).
- **Rules:** staff/admin MFA; controlled exports + retention; clinical/financial/HR/candidate data segregated.
- **Acceptance:** unauthorized actions denied and logged; access changes auditable.

### 8.2 Reports & analytics
- **Inputs:** report type (operations, clinical services, finance, pharmacy, recruitment, engagement); filters (date, branch, department, category, status); data sources (source + refresh timestamp); export (PDF; Excel/CSV where enabled).
- **Flow:** select report + filters → validate user scope, retrieve → display with data freshness + definitions → export authorized results, **log export**.
- **Outputs:** Operations (occupancy, length of stay, OPD/IPD, emergency, surgery counts); Clinical (doctor/department performance, lab turnaround, report status); Finance (revenue, collections, dues, expenses, claims/rejections); Inventory (stock, expiry, low stock, fast-moving); Recruitment/engagement (vacancies, pipeline, notice reach/ack, campaign metrics).
- **Rules:** dashboards distinguish live vs sample/mock; exports follow role permissions + privacy.
- **Acceptance:** filters apply consistently; exported data equals displayed authorized results.

### 8.3 Security, privacy, clinical safeguards
- **Inputs:** authentication (OTP/SMS, password reset, staff/admin MFA); session/device (timeout, auto-logout, device management); data (encryption in transit + at rest, backups, DR); consent (text/version, purpose, timestamp); audit events (record views, create/update/delete, clinical/financial changes).
- **Flow:** authenticate + authorize every request by role and workflow context → encryption, session controls, secure document handling → capture consent, enforce purpose/access rules → log sensitive access/changes; monitor/review → retention, backup, recovery procedures.
- **Outputs:** access decisions, audit records, alerts; consent + data-access history; backup/restore + DR capability.
- **Rules:** align with DPDP Act (India) / HIPAA (US) where applicable — make compliance controls configurable and flag for legal validation; emergency workflows always accessible; promotions never obstruct care.
- **Acceptance:** sensitive actions auditable; unauthorized access blocked; **recovery procedures tested** (include a restore test script).

### 8.4 Integrations & interoperability
- **Adapters (each with interface + mock implementation + manual fallback):** Payment gateway (payment, refund, receipt, reconciliation); Messaging SMS/email/WhatsApp (templates, recipient consent, delivery status); Insurance/schemes — Insurer/TPA/ABDM (eligibility, pre-auth, claim, status); Diagnostics — Analyzer/PACS/DICOM (orders, results, images); Health interoperability HL7/FHIR (mapped clinical data + identity); Location/devices — Maps, ambulance dispatch, wearables (permissioned); External providers (API/webhook/portal/manual).
- **Flow:** confirm scope/agreement/credentials/data mapping → exchange via approved secure interface → validate response, update module **idempotently** → log errors, retry where safe, manual fallback → monitor freshness, availability, ownership, support SLA.
- **Outputs:** updated source module with provider references; **visible failed/pending integration queue**; monitoring (status, latency, freshness, audit logs).
- **Acceptance:** integration failure is visible and **never silently loses or duplicates transactions** (use outbox pattern, idempotency keys, dead-letter queue).

