## 11. NON-NEGOTIABLE CROSS-CUTTING REQUIREMENTS (checklist)

- [ ] Every create/update/delete and every sensitive view is audit-logged (user, action, timestamp, before/after).
- [ ] Patient data strictly scoped to the patient (or authorized dependent); staff data scoped by role + branch.
- [ ] No raw card data stored; gateway tokenization/redirect only; idempotent callbacks; unique transaction references.
- [ ] No double-booking of slots; no overlapping bed assignments; no dispensing above stock without authorized exception; no blood issue without authorization; no clinical staffing deployment before credential checks; no Ready room before inspection pass; no PO without approval; closed/expired vacancies reject applications; expired notices/campaigns auto-stop.
- [ ] Unreviewed results never shown as diagnosis; lab status doesn't imply interpretation; dispatch status/ETA shown only when confirmed by dispatch.
- [ ] Stale/unconfirmed external data is always labelled; never shown as live.
- [ ] Error messages never leak whether an account exists or expose sensitive details.
- [ ] Emergency SOS always prominent, accessible, with call fallback, never obstructed by ads.
- [ ] Sample/mock values labelled; dashboards show live vs delayed vs mock.
- [ ] Empty states, loading states, error states, pagination on all lists.
- [ ] Notifications (push/email/SMS/in-app) via templates, honoring consent and preferred channel.
- [ ] Accessibility, localization-ready strings, responsive layouts.

